Differences from the lab guide
------------------------------
* SonarQube already runs on SQ1, so skip "docker compose up -d sonarqube".
  http://localhost:9000 on SC1 reaches it, which means tools\scan-sonar.ps1
  works unchanged. First login: admin / admin, then set a throwaway password.
* tools\verify-env.ps1 reports docker as MISSING on SC1. That is expected:
  in this sandbox Docker runs on SQ1 and OWZ1. Use verify-cr-env.ps1 instead.
* ZAP runs on another machine, so it cannot reach 127.0.0.1 on SC1. The
  application still binds to 127.0.0.1 only. SC1 forwards port 8080 on
  {{ cr14_ip_sc1 }} to it, and the Windows firewall admits that port from OWZ1
  ({{ cr14_ip_owz1 }}) and nothing else. Do not change server.address.
* To look at the containers:  ssh {{ cr14_trainee_user }}@sq1   or   ssh {{ cr14_trainee_user }}@owz1
  then:  cd /opt/cr14 && docker compose ps

